  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 142 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe latter half of the work week may start off on a cloudy note \nThursday, due to the continued cyclonic flow over the region and \nupper trof effects. Some guidance suggests we could even see some \nsunshine Thursday, but with the upper-level system/cyclonic flow \nstill in place, have leaned towards a mostly cloudy forecast. Some \nsctrd showers continue to look to occur Thursday and into Thursday \nevening under the passing upper trof axis. Things look to fully dry \nout by Friday as an area of high pressure and upper-level ridging \ndevelop and build acrs the region. If skies can clear out along with \na sfc wind decouple, Friday night into Saturday morning should have \nlow temps well down in the 30s.\n\nAs we look ahead towards the upcoming weekend into early next week, \nthere's not much of note, thanks to an amplified upper-level ridge \nthat's progged to develop over the Intermountain West states. This \nwill help block any shortwaves from translating over our region, \nresulting in a dry forecast. Average to slightly above average \ntemperatures will be common during this time frame, with highs in \nthe middle to upper 50s and lows in the upper 30s. Return flow \nwarming may help produce another round of well above temps back into \nthe 60s for Monday.",
